# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file. It is here because the
# citable artefact of this project is not only the code: docs/BENCHMARKS.md and
# docs/running-the-benchmarks.md publish a measurement methodology (licence-checked corpora,
# revision-pinned datasets, a per-suite published/not-published column), and docs/adr/ is a
# decision log with the rejected alternatives written down. Those are things a reader cites.
#
# NOTE ON `version` / `date-released`: deliberately absent. No release has been cut and no
# `v*` tag exists (see CHANGELOG.md and RELEASE-GATES.md), so a version here would be the
# same false claim CHANGELOG.md's 0.1.0 entry had to be corrected for. They go in when the
# first tag is cut, per docs/RELEASING.md.
#
# NOTE ON `license`: the SPDX identifier is Apache-2.0 (ADR-0063, which supersedes the
# PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0 relicence of ADR-0055). It stays expressed as `license-url`
# rather than `license`: the CFF 1.2.0 schema validates `license` against an SPDX enum frozen
# at schema-release time, and the URL form points at the authoritative text shipped in this
# repository, which is what a citing reader should resolve. `Apache-2.0` is in that enum, so
# the `license` key would now validate — but the URL is the stronger claim (it cites the
# file, not a label) and switching keys would gain nothing.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this framework, or the measurements and decisions published with it, please cite it as below."
title: "Latence Framework: messy enterprise documents to AI-ready data"
abstract: >-
  A model-agnostic, cloud-agnostic framework that turns messy, siloed enterprise documents into
  PII-handled, embedded, provenance-carrying RAG corpora and evidence-linked knowledge graphs.
  Every Stage declares typed input/output contracts and is fulfilled by a swappable Provider.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dickmann
    given-names: Dennis
    email: ddickmann81@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/ddickmann/latence-framework"
url: "https://ddickmann.github.io/latence-framework/"
license-url: "https://github.com/ddickmann/latence-framework/blob/main/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - ai-ready-data
  - knowledge-graph
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - entity-resolution
  - pii-redaction
  - data-pipeline
